  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Developing rights-based and empowering approaches to mobilise (DREAM) ACTION TO</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The majority of women in Gambia (76%) and Sierra Leone (88%) are affected by FGM. The project will address this using a community based approach working directly with young women and their communities to provide services and protection and help young women take action together as well as seek attitude change in communities. At the same time it will work in both countries to seek more widespread change by advocating for the creation and implementation of legal frameworks that ensure that girls and young women are protected from FGM. This approach will work with four different partners and draw upon their range of expertise to tackle this complex issue.</narrative>
  </description>
